===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|telt|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|teld||tent|lang=ang}}, influenced by {{etyl|da}} {{term|telt|lang=da}} <ref>{{R:Webster 1913|tilt}}</ref>(, from {{etyl|gml}} {{term|telt|lang=gml}}), or directly from Middle Low German<ref>[http://ordnet.dk/ods/opslag?opslag=telt&submit=S%F8g Etymology] in [[:w:da:ODS|ODS]]</ref>. Cognates include German {{term|Zelt||tent}}, Old Norse {{term|tjald||tent}} ( > archaic Danish {{term|tjæld||tent}}). More at {{l|en|teld}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# a [[canvas]] covering for carts etc. {{defdate|1450}}

